@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: EXPERIMENT — where do Android/iOS emulators live for an sbx agent: in the box, or on the host?
' status: measured 2026-09-29/30; built as _spec/internal/sbx/host-android-adb.puml
'   what was built ................... _spec/internal/sbx/host-android-adb.puml
'   the pattern it copies ............ _spec/internal/sbx/host-browser-cdp.puml
'   why the box has no /dev/kvm ...... _spec/_experiments/nested-sbx-kvm.puml
'   the host-side egress bypass ...... _spec/_experiments/cdp-shared-browser.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── SOURCES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   mobile-mcp       : https://github.com/mobile-next/mobile-mcp
'   mobilecli        : https://github.com/mobile-next/mobilecli
'   idb architecture : https://github.com/facebook/idb/blob/main/website/docs/idb/architecture.mdx
'   idb remote       : https://github.com/facebook/idb/blob/main/website/docs/idb/installation.mdx
'   emulator on arm64: https://gist.github.com/atyachin/2f7c6054c4cd6945397165a23623987d
'
' ── Q1: CAN THE EMULATOR LIVE INSIDE sbx? NO ────────────────────────────────
'   emulator (hvf/kvm)  needs /dev/kvm; the box has none (nested-sbx-kvm.puml)
'   redroid             needs binder + CAP_SYS_ADMIN; CapEff is 0x0
'   cuttlefish          needs /dev/kvm
'   pure TCG            [Speculation] boots, at >10x the 52 s hvf boot
' Every in-box route fails on the runtime, not the image. Same floor as E1.
'
' ── Q2: HOST BRIDGE, MEASURED ON THIS HOST (M4 Pro, macOS 26.7) ────────────
'   emulator 36.4.9 · AVD Medium_Phone_API_36.1 (Play, release-keys, no root)
'   -accel-check                     hvf OK
'   -no-window -no-audio boot        52 s to sys.boot_completed=1
'   listeners                        127.0.0.1:5037 adb server
'                                    127.0.0.1:5554 emulator CONSOLE
'                                    127.0.0.1:5555 emulator adbd
'   raw host:version  -> 5037        OKAY 0029
'   raw host:devices-l -> 5037       OKAY emulator-5554 device
'   fresh adbkey -> 5555 direct      unauthorized
'   same, with -skip-adb-auth        unauthorized (Play image ignores it)
' So the ADB SERVER is the reachable seam; the key never leaves the host.
'
' ── MEASURED FROM A GUEST (sbx v0.42.1, per-sandbox allow localhost:5037) ──
'   raw host:version  -> 169.254.1.1:5037            OKAY 0029, 18.5 ms
'   raw host:devices-l -> host.docker.internal:5037  OKAY emulator-5554
'   policy log                                       localhost:5037 transparent
'   adbutils AdbClient(host=169.254.1.1)
'     get_state            device
'     am start SETTINGS    mCurrentFocus = SettingsHomepageActivity
'     screenshot           1080x2400 in 0.96 s
'     uiautomator dump     30 071 bytes in 2.59 s
'   Ubuntu adb 34.0.5 via ADB_SERVER_SOCKET  devices + shell OK, no local
'                                            server, host server pid unchanged
' Unlike Chrome, ADB ignores Host, so the hostname works too; the IP stays
' canonical for parity with hostcdp.
'
' ── LIFECYCLE: THE hostcdp SHAPE, ONE FOR ONE ──────────────────────────────
'   hostcdp (hermes)                      hostadb (android)
'   Ready: GET :9222/json/version         Ready: host:devices lists a serial
'   reuse whatever answers                reuse any running emulator
'   launch Chrome --user-data-dir=        launch emulator -avd <avd>
'     UserConfigDir/proveo/host-chrome      (PROVEO_HOST_AVD, else the first)
'   own process group, left open          own process group, left open
'   env BROWSER_CDP_URL=http://<ip>:P     env ADB_SERVER_SOCKET=tcp:<ip>:5037
'   Kit allow localhost:<port>            Kit allow localhost:5037
' Windowed launch lets the operator watch and log in once; AVD userdata
' persists the login across runs, as the Chrome profile does.
'
' ── THREE ROUTES; DECIDED 2026-09-29: RAW 5037 ─────────────────────────────
'   raw      ADB_SERVER_SOCKET=tcp:<gateway ip>:5037  key on host · host dials  ← chosen
'   relay    same, via a host relay that drops connect/kill/reverse  (deferred)
'   in-VM    VM adb server -> <gateway ip>:5555  host adbkey copied into VM ✗
' Raw mirrors hostcdp: dial the gateway by IP, one Kit allow, env only, and a
' run-time warning carries the risk, as it does for host Chrome.
'
' ── THE HOLE RAW 5037 OPENS, ACCEPTED BY WARNING ───────────────────────────
' An adb server is a host-side dialer. `host:connect:<ip>:<port>` makes the
' HOST open a TCP connection, outside sbx egress. `reverse` lets the device
' reach host loopback. The emulator's own network is the host's NAT, so an
' agent browsing inside Android is outside policy — the host-Chrome case again.
' Deferred mitigation: a host relay forwarding only
'   host:version  host:devices[-l]  host:track-devices  host:transport:<serial>
'   host:list-forward
' and refusing connect/disconnect/kill/reverse; plus `-http-proxy` on launch.
'
' ── THE DRIVER: PRIMITIVES ON THE HARNESS'S MODEL ─────────────────────────
' mobile-mcp 1.0.6 exposes tools, not an agent: tap, swipe, type, element
' list, screenshot, app launch, buttons. The harness's own model reasons over
' them, so the add-on adds no provider, no key and no second loop.
'   default (mobilecli)   element list + tap need an on-device server reached
'                         by `adb forward`; behind the remote server that
'                         listener lands on the HOST's loopback → "device
'                         server did not start" until forwards are mirrored
'   MOBILEMCP_LEGACY_ROBOT=1  plain adb shell: launch, screenshot, tap, HOME
'                         work; element list fails — `uiautomator dump
'                         /dev/tty` is Killed on API 36, on the host too
' A VM-side mirror (host:list-forward, then host:transport + the forward's own
' target per connection) made the default mode whole: launch, elements, tap,
' type, screenshot, foreground app, HOME. Built as internal/adbmirror.
'
' ── Q3: CAN THE NERDBOX (non-macOS) RUN AN iOS SIMULATOR? NO ───────────────
' Simulator runtimes are macOS frameworks shipped only in Xcode; Apple's
' licence confines macOS to Apple hardware. Reachable iOS for a Linux host:
'   remote Mac     idb_companion on macOS :10882; the idb CLI is pure Python
'                  and runs anywhere — the same seam shape as the adb server
'   cloud          Corellium (virtual iOS), BrowserStack/Appetize (streamed)
' mobile-mcp lists iOS Simulators too, on a macOS host with Xcode.
' Android on the nerdbox is fine: the host emulator runs on KVM, same bridge.
'
' ── RECOMMENDATION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Host bridge, raw 5037, warned. "Fully inside sbx + attach" is the preferred
' UX but is gated by the same upstream sbx feature as E1 (/dev/kvm into the
' VM). Revisit when docker/sbx-releases ships device passthrough; until then
' `attach` = attach to the HOST emulator.
'
' ── HYPOTHESES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' H1  PASS  guest raw host:version -> 169.254.1.1:5037
' H2  PASS  adbutils via the gateway: launch, screenshot, hierarchy
' H3  PASS  mobile-mcp through the gateway + adb-mirror, e2e on the rebuilt
'           image (host server pid unchanged)
' H4  open  a real harness session driving the emulator through mobile-mcp
' H5  open  (if the relay is revived) it refuses host:connect and passes H3
' H6  [Unverified] whether sbx enforces the Kit allow on the direct path
' ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

title Experiment — mobile device reach: in the box, or bridged to the host

node "macOS host (M4 Pro)" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "Android emulator\nhvf · 52 s boot" as EMU <<app>>
  component "adb server\n127.0.0.1:5037" as ADB <<app>>
  component "iOS Simulator\nXcode only" as SIM <<async>>
}

node "sbx microVM" as VM <<host>> {
  component "mobile-mcp + adb-mirror\nADB_SERVER_SOCKET=tcp:169.254.1.1:5037" as MCP <<app>>
  component "in-box emulator\nno /dev/kvm · CapEff 0x0" as INBOX <<error>>
}

node "nerdbox (Linux)" as NERD <<cloud>> {
  component "iOS Simulator\nnot possible" as NOSIM <<error>>
}

MCP ARROW_MAIN ADB : ADB over gateway IP · Kit allow localhost:5037
ADB ARROW_MAIN EMU : emulator-5554
MCP ARROW_QUEUE SIM : coming soon — not built
MCP ARROW_ERROR INBOX : blocked by the runtime
NERD ARROW_QUEUE SIM : remote Mac over network

note bottom of MCP
  **The server is the seam, not adbd.** A fresh
  key on :5555 reads unauthorized, even with
  -skip-adb-auth on a Play image; :5037 answers
  OKAY and keeps the adbkey on the host.
end note

note bottom of ADB
  **An adb server dials for you.** host:connect
  opens a host TCP socket outside sbx egress;
  the run warns, as host CDP does, and a relay
  that drops connect stays the deferred fix.
end note

note bottom of INBOX
  **The floor is the runtime again.** No
  /dev/kvm, zero caps, no binder: emulator,
  redroid and cuttlefish all stop at the same
  gate nested-sbx-kvm.puml already measured.
end note

note bottom of NOSIM
  **iOS needs a Mac somewhere.** Simulator
  runtimes ship only in Xcode on macOS; a Linux
  host reaches iOS through a remote Mac's
  idb_companion or a cloud device.
end note

note bottom of SIM
  **Same seam, one release later.** Simulators
  run beside the Android emulator on the Mac;
  idb's companion on :10882 or mobile-mcp's
  iOS path would reach them from the VM.
end note

@enduml
